Downloads follow the usual pair:

in ui.R, downloadButton("id", "Label")
in server.R, output$id &lt;- downloadHandler(...)

output$downloadSummary &lt;- downloadHandler(
1  filename = function() {
    paste0("descriptive-", input$dataset, ".csv")
  },
2  content = function(file) {
    write.csv(ddata(), file, row.names = FALSE)
  }
)

1

A function that returns the name of the file the user will get

2

A function that writes the content into file (a temporary path chosen by Shiny)


For a plot, content opens a graphic device, draws the plot and closes the device:
content = function(file) {
  png(file, width = 800, height = 600)
  plot(dataInput()[, 1:2])
  dev.off()
}
