## file: ui.R
library(shiny)

ui &lt;- fluidPage(
  sidebarLayout(
    sidebarPanel(
      selectInput("dataset", "Choose a dataset:",
                  choices = c("rock", "pressure", "cars")),
      actionButton("load", "Select dataset")
    ),
    mainPanel(
      plotOutput("graph"),
      downloadButton("downloadPlot", "Download plot"),
      verbatimTextOutput("summary"),
      downloadButton("downloadSummary", "Download summary")
    )
  )
)

## file: server.R
library(shiny)

server &lt;- function(input, output, session) {

  dataInput &lt;- eventReactive(input$load, {
    switch(input$dataset,
           rock = rock,
           pressure = pressure,
           cars = cars)
  })

  # descriptive statistics of the first two columns
  ddata &lt;- reactive({
    df &lt;- dataInput()[, 1:2]
    data.frame(variable = names(df),
               mean = sapply(df, mean),
               sd = sapply(df, sd),
               row.names = NULL)
  })

  output$graph &lt;- renderPlot({
    plot(dataInput()[, 1:2])
  })

  output$summary &lt;- renderPrint({
    ddata()
  })

  # downloadHandler = the "render" function of downloadButton()
  output$downloadSummary &lt;- downloadHandler(
    filename = function() {
      paste0("descriptive-", input$dataset, ".csv")
    },
    content = function(file) {
      write.csv(ddata(), file, row.names = FALSE)
    }
  )

  output$downloadPlot &lt;- downloadHandler(
    filename = function() {
      paste0("plot-", input$dataset, ".png")
    },
    content = function(file) {
      png(file, width = 800, height = 600)
      plot(dataInput()[, 1:2])
      dev.off()
    }
  )
}







Exercise



Add a download button to your explore-a-dataset app that saves newdata() as a CSV file.

The two pieces
# ui.R
1actionButton("load", "Select dataset")

1

A button with ID load. Remember: input$load is a counter that increases at every click


# server.R
1dataInput &lt;- eventReactive(input$load, {
2  if (input$dataset == 1) {
    rock
  } else if (input$dataset == 2) {
    pressure
  } else {
    cars
  }
})

1

The first argument is the trigger: the code runs only when input$load changes, i.e., when the button is clicked

2

The code to run. It reads input$dataset, but changing the dataset does not trigger it: its value is simply read at the moment of the click


dataInput() is then used exactly as a reactive(): data &lt;- dataInput() inside the render*() functions.

The app
Change the dataset: nothing happens. Click the button: now it does.
#| '!! shinylive warning !!': |
#|   shinylive does not work in self-contained HTML documents.
#|   Please set `embed-resources: false` in your metadata.
#| standalone: true
#| components: [editor, viewer]
#| layout: vertical
#| viewerHeight: 650
## file: ui.R
library(shiny)

ui &lt;- fluidPage(
  sidebarLayout(
    sidebarPanel(
      selectInput(
        inputId = "dataset",
        label = "Choose a dataset:",
        choices = list("rock" = 1, "pressure" = 2, "cars" = 3)
      ),
      actionButton("load", "Select dataset")
    ),
    mainPanel(
      plotOutput("graph"),
      verbatimTextOutput("summary")
    )
  )
)

## file: server.R
library(shiny)

server &lt;- function(input, output, session) {

  # runs ONLY when the button is clicked
  dataInput &lt;- eventReactive(input$load, {
    if (input$dataset == 1) {
      rock
    } else if (input$dataset == 2) {
      pressure
    } else {
      cars
    }
  })

  output$graph &lt;- renderPlot({
    data &lt;- dataInput()
    plot(data[, 1:2])
  })

  output$summary &lt;- renderPrint({
    data &lt;- dataInput()
    summary(data[, 1:2])
  })
}

Notice also that before the first click the outputs are empty: at the start the button has never been clicked, so eventReactive() has no value yet, and the outputs that need it wait silently.

The UI is a web page
fluidPage(), selectInput() & co. are R functions that write HTML for you. Try this in the console:
library(shiny)
selectInput(inputId = "mySelection", label = "Select box",
            choices = c("Choice 1" = 1, "Choice 2" = 2))
R prints (shortened):
&lt;div class="form-group shiny-input-container"&gt;
  &lt;label class="control-label" for="mySelection"&gt;Select box&lt;/label&gt;
  &lt;select id="mySelection"&gt;
    &lt;option value="1" selected&gt;Choice 1&lt;/option&gt;
    &lt;option value="2"&gt;Choice 2&lt;/option&gt;
  &lt;/select&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
So the UI contains two kinds of elements:

Inputs (*Input(), actionButton()…): the controls the user plays with
Outputs (*Output()): empty boxes, each with a name, waiting for the server to fill them

Each element is identified by its ID (id="mySelection"). Remember this: the ID is the only thing the server knows about the UI.

Server
ui = fluidPage(
selectInput(inputId = "mySelection",
            label = h3("Select box"),
    choices = list("Choice 1" = 1, "Choice 2" = 2, "Choice 3" = 3),
    selected = 1),

  verbatimTextOutput(
  outputId = "myOutput"
)

)

server = function(input, output) {
  output$myOutput = renderText({
    paste(paste("This is my choice"), input$mySelection)
  })
}

Step 1 · Load a dataset
Nothing new here: a menu, a button, an eventReactive(). We print the first rows to check that the data arrive.
