## file: ui.R
library(shiny)

ui &lt;- fluidPage(
  titlePanel("Explore a dataset"),
  sidebarLayout(
    sidebarPanel(
      selectInput(
        "dataset",
        "Choose a dataset:",
        choices = c("rock" = 1, "pressure" = 2, "cars" = 3)
      ),
      actionButton("load", "Load dataset")
    ),
    mainPanel(
      verbatimTextOutput("preview")
    )
  )
)

## file: server.R
library(shiny)

server &lt;- function(input, output, session) {

  # 1. LOAD THE DATASET (only when "Load dataset" is clicked)
  dataInput &lt;- eventReactive(input$load, {
    if (input$dataset == 1) {
      rock
    } else if (input$dataset == 2) {
      pressure
    } else {
      cars
    }
  })

  # check that the data arrived
  output$preview &lt;- renderPrint({
    head(dataInput())
  })
}

Step 2 · Menus built from the data
The X and Y menus cannot be written in ui.R: their choices are the column names, and we know them only after the data are loaded. So:

in ui.R we reserve an empty slot with uiOutput()
in server.R, renderUI() creates the selectInput() and puts it in that slot

# ui.R
1uiOutput("x_ui")

1

An empty slot for a piece of UI that the server will create


# server.R
1vars &lt;- reactive({
  names(dataInput())
})

2output$x_ui &lt;- renderUI({
3  selectInput("x", "X variable:",
              choices = vars(),
              selected = vars()[1])
})

1

The column names, as a reactive expression: they change when new data are loaded

2

renderUI() is the partner of uiOutput()

3

A normal selectInput(), with ID x: from now on the server can read input$x, like any other input


