## file: ui.R
library(shiny)

ui &lt;- fluidPage(
  titlePanel("Explore a dataset"),
  sidebarLayout(
    sidebarPanel(
      selectInput(
        "dataset",
        "Choose a dataset:",
        choices = c("rock" = 1, "pressure" = 2, "cars" = 3)
      ),
      actionButton("load", "Load dataset"),
      hr(),
      uiOutput("x_ui"),
      uiOutput("y_ui"),
      actionButton("analyze", "Update analysis")   # NEW: second button
    ),
    mainPanel(
      plotOutput("graph"),                         # NEW
      verbatimTextOutput("summary")                # NEW
    )
  )
)

## file: server.R
library(shiny)

server &lt;- function(input, output, session) {

  # 1. LOAD THE DATASET
  dataInput &lt;- eventReactive(input$load, {
    if (input$dataset == 1) {
      rock
    } else if (input$dataset == 2) {
      pressure
    } else {
      cars
    }
  })

  # 2. VARIABLE NAMES
  vars &lt;- reactive({
    names(dataInput())
  })

  # 3. DYNAMIC UI
  output$x_ui &lt;- renderUI({
    selectInput("x", "X variable:",
                choices = vars(),
                selected = vars()[1])
  })

  output$y_ui &lt;- renderUI({
    selectInput("y", "Y variable:",
                choices = vars(),
                selected = vars()[min(2, length(vars()))])
  })

  # 4. DATA FOR THE ANALYSIS (NEW): frozen until "Update analysis" is clicked
  newdata &lt;- eventReactive(input$analyze, {
    df &lt;- dataInput()
    df[, c(input$x, input$y), drop = FALSE]
  })

  # 5. OUTPUTS (NEW)
  output$graph &lt;- renderPlot({
    df &lt;- newdata()
    x &lt;- df[[1]]
    y &lt;- df[[2]]
    if (is.factor(x) || is.character(x)) {
      boxplot(y ~ x, xlab = names(df)[1], ylab = names(df)[2])
    } else {
      plot(x, y, xlab = names(df)[1], ylab = names(df)[2], pch = 19)
    }
  })

  output$summary &lt;- renderPrint({
    summary(newdata())
  })
}

Try it: load cars, choose the variables, click Update analysis. Now change the variables without clicking: the plot does not move until you click again.

Step 4 · Upload your own data
Last step: a fourth option, Upload data. When it is selected, a file input and the choice of the column separator appear.
1conditionalPanel(
2  condition = "input.dataset == '4'",
  fileInput("file", "Select a CSV file", accept = ".csv"),
  radioButtons("sep", "Column separator",
               choices = c(";" = ";", "," = ","))
)

1

Shows its content only when the condition is true

2

The condition is written in JavaScript, not in R: input.dataset with a dot, and '4' in quotes (remember: the value of a selectInput() is text)


And in the server, a fourth case in dataInput():
} else {
1  req(input$file)
2  read.csv(input$file$datapath, sep = input$sep)
}

1

req() = required: if no file has been uploaded yet, stop here silently, without an error

2

Read the file from the place where Shiny saved it, with the separator chosen by the user


Test files: example.csv (separator ,) and example-semicolon.csv (separator ;).
